    "q-109860": {
      "dom_id": "step-q109860",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Let $A$ be a $4\\times 6$ matrix. What is the image of ${R}^{4}$ under the action of ${A}^{T}?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that ${A}^{T}$ is a $6\\times 4$ matrix.\n\nPre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{4}$ by ${A}^{T}$ gives a linear combination of the columns of ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1}^{T} & {a}_{2}^{T} & {a}_{3}^{T} & {a}_{4}^{T} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{T}}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{1}^{T} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{2}^{T} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{3}^{T} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{4}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {a}_{4}^{T} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{4}$ under the action of ${A}^{T}$ must be $\\text{Col}({A}^{T}),$ the row space of $A.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
