    "q-109877": {
      "dom_id": "step-q109877",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Consider a $3\\times 2$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{dim}(\\text{Col}({A}^{T}))=2,$ then $\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A))=$",
      "worked_solution": "The four fundamental subspaces of a matrix $A$ can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14198391/assets/889b83fadd26b377c4dd34143c9b16541630c04e90de3d9b005e7147ead75ad5.png)\n\nIn our case, we are given that $m=3,$ $n=2,$ and $r=2.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(A)) & =n-r=2-2=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
